ool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 376395, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011di46RwMLfb5hqYvpjis7Y", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 380833, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and the pull request is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says banker's rounding. So 2.665 came out as 2.67, and the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On the branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). The import changed to match; nothing else did.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **Pull request:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't check what FIN-212 says, because the advisory lookup tool doesn't recognise that ID. The fix is based only on the test and the docstring.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01H2AzcqMAb9uVoRyS32AvPu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GSHcQeCPoYxPjN9uGP5urf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Sbkx6VE9tAKaCWzve9FEv6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HkWUA9azF6fMoxFM3s9AaC", "caller": {"t