urn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and the pull request is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its docstring says banker's rounding. So 2.665 came out as 2.67, and the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On the branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). The import changed to match; nothing else did.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **Pull request:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't check what FIN-212 says, because the advisory lookup tool doesn't recognise that ID. The fix is based only on the test and the docstring.", "type": "text"}]}]}